Tim Hawks:

2
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:06.029
Good morning. We are going to start receiving man plans next week.

3
00:00:06.029 --> 00:00:20.765
You do not have to have them in for another month, but the sooner you guys turn them in, the sooner we will get our team working on giving you some feedback and getting them back to you.

4
00:00:20.765 --> 00:00:40.888
And so some of you are saying, "What is a man plan?" Well, we talked about this a couple weeks ago, and there is actually an outline for how to go about writing one, and it is basically developing a plan for how you are going to grow in your masculinity.

5
00:00:40.888 --> 00:00:57.446
For some of you, it might be done on a napkin or the back of a business card. For others of you, it might be a novel, just depending on what you need to say and do. But I want to encourage you guys to do that.

6
00:00:57.446 --> 00:01:13.767
If you do not have the plan, grab Nate. He can get that in your hands. Or if you are in one of our other venues, feel free to talk to whoever is leading that venue and get started on it as soon as possible.

7
00:01:13.767 --> 00:01:30.404
Let me just start off this morning by saying much of what you hear on a day-to-day basis is not true. Hopefully you guys know that by now. You do know that, right? So, for example, the so-called gender pay gap.

8
00:01:30.404 --> 00:01:42.922
You guys know that that is a myth, right? Okay. You do not know that is a myth? That women make about 22 percent less than what men do? That is just not true.

9
00:01:42.922 --> 00:01:53.300
It has not been true for a long time, but it gets said over and over and over again. It is a way for power people to win elections.

10
00:01:53.300 --> 00:02:10.730
You say, "Well, tell me a little bit more about that." Well, let me give you just a couple sources. Freakonomics.com. Spend some time there. You will find out that there is a lot of stuff that gets said that is not true.

11
00:02:10.730 --> 00:02:23.881
"The True Story of the Gender Pay Gap," January 7, 2016. Or if you want to go to Forbes.com, April 16, 2012, "It is Time to End the Pay Gap Myth," written by a woman.

12
00:02:23.881 --> 00:02:28.951
So that stuff is not true, but it gets said over and over again.

13
00:02:28.951 --> 00:02:35.368
Well, here is another one. "The Quran does not teach violence." That is not true.

14
00:02:35.368 --> 00:02:46.459
Yesterday we saw an expression of people carrying out things that are in the Quran and things that were carried out by the prophet Muhammad.

15
00:02:46.459 --> 00:03:00.007
Now, if I say that, people say, "Well, that is Islamophobia." Well, having an irrational fear, which is phobia, of Islam is only real if there is no rational basis for it.

16
00:03:00.007 --> 00:03:18.229
So read USA Today opinion yesterday, March 22, 2016, "The Quran's Deadly Role in Inspiring the Belgian Slaughter." And you will see Nabeel Qureshi lay out a case from the Quran and the Hadith that that is what it actually teaches.

17
00:03:18.229 --> 00:03:32.490
In fact, I am reading a whole book right now on the Crusades and all the myths that we have been taught about the Crusades. Much of what you hear on a day-to-day basis is not true.

18
00:03:32.490 --> 00:03:57.684
You say, "Why are you starting with this?" The reason why I am starting with this is because when it comes to human thriving, when it comes to happiness, when it comes to being masculine, when it comes to being feminine, when it comes to raising daughters, much if not most of what you hear today actually is not true.

19
00:03:57.684 --> 00:04:15.034
It does not correspond to reality. And so the really cool thing as a Christian is my faith challenges me to use reason, to look at the rational world around me, to gather evidence, to look at science, to read, to think.

20
00:04:15.034 --> 00:04:28.978
That is the nature of Christianity. In fact the rational Western mindset grew out of Christianity. And so I am not simply told to just read a book and ignore what is around me.

21
00:04:28.978 --> 00:04:39.039
I am told to read a book and look at what is around me because if the Bible is true, you will see it all around you. And it is.

22
00:04:39.039 --> 00:04:54.092
And so today, we are going to talk about raising daughters. And I am going to say some things today that you are going to go, "Really? Really? You are kidding me, right?" No, I am not. Okay.

23
00:04:54.092 --> 00:05:09.541
So we are going to dive in here. And some of you are saying, "Well, you know, I am not a dad. I do not have a daughter." In fact, how many of you guys do have daughters? Yeah, quite a few of you.

24
00:05:09.541 --> 00:05:14.453
Some of you guys are going to say, "You know, I am a teenager.

25
00:05:14.453 --> 00:05:30.615
What has this got to do with me?" It has got a lot to do with you because we are talking about whether these guys that have daughters are going to raise your wife [snorts] in a way that is helpful to you.

26
00:05:30.615 --> 00:05:36.398
You will understand women a little bit better as we go through the study.

27
00:05:36.398 --> 00:05:49.232
So let us talk about daughters. Characteristics of daughters. First of all, when it comes to our daughters, I would suggest that daughters have natural strengths.

28
00:05:49.232 --> 00:06:05.553
And those strengths would demonstrate that daughters are actually more stable than sons. More stable than sons. Some of you say, "Whoa, wait a minute. I am a son." Okay, hopefully everyone in here is a son.

29
00:06:05.553 --> 00:06:15.060
How can you say that? Well, let me give you three reasons. First of all, their course of development is less disruptive.

30
00:06:15.060 --> 00:06:30.271
We have talked about boys having to break that overly bonded connection to mom at some point where they move from being boys to being men. When it comes to daughters, that never has to happen.

31
00:06:30.271 --> 00:06:42.789
They can maintain that relationship with the person of their gender throughout life and they never have to work through the power issues associated with that.

32
00:06:42.789 --> 00:06:53.801
Second, girls are more physically healthy than boys. Women live longer. They have less disease. They are actually more emotionally healthy.

33
00:06:53.801 --> 00:07:07.507
And some of you are saying, "Whoa, wait a minute." Women tend to flutter emotionally when boys tend to fall. And so women have a tendency to kind of have more ups and downs.

34
00:07:07.507 --> 00:07:20.738
And it is more normal when you see it, but they tend to do that within a normal range. When boys have psychological or emotional problems, they tend to be very severe.

35
00:07:20.738 --> 00:07:36.583
Here is the third one. Women commit fewer crimes, fewer suicides, fewer disruptions. Women have a tendency when it comes to suicide to [snorts] attempt suicide. Boys have a tendency to commit suicide.

36
00:07:36.583 --> 00:07:52.270
And lest you think this is a teenage problem, the highest rate of suicide in the United States is men between 50 and 55. Between 50 and 55. Some of you are saying, "Yeah, I am kind of in that range.

37
00:07:52.270 --> 00:08:09.304
I am kind of in that risk area." It is a huge, huge issue for men. When men get depressed, it goes really, really bad. Women tend to get help. Men tend to get isolated. And so there are some natural strengths there.

38
00:08:09.304 --> 00:08:18.019
Secondly, there are some personal strengths. Daughters are more personally secure than sons in their identity.

39
00:08:18.019 --> 00:08:31.091
Every day that a girl wakes up, she is reminded that she has a contribution that she can make to the world that is world-changing. Her body, her breasts, her uterus.

40
00:08:31.091 --> 00:08:43.529
She knows that she has something special that she can do, and that is raise children. She can nurture the next generation. She can bring life into the world.

41
00:08:43.529 --> 00:09:00.721
And so she has got an identity that is built into the fabric of her body. Boys, on the other hand, have muscles. What do you do with those muscles? Do you use them to beat up the kid down the street or bully somebody?

42
00:09:00.721 --> 00:09:09.277
Do you use those muscles to build a bridge? Do you use those muscles to become a great athlete or a warrior?

43
00:09:09.277 --> 00:09:19.735
In other words, the testosterone and the frame and the muscles and who you are as a man does not speak very loudly to your identity.

44
00:09:19.735 --> 00:09:35.263
And that is why Margaret Mead said the biggest challenge that every society has is to define appropriate roles for men. You have got the energy, you have got the power, but what do you do with it?

45
00:09:35.263 --> 00:09:40.967
And so daughters are more personally secure in their identity than sons.

46
00:09:40.967 --> 00:09:56.574
Now, daughters also face huge challenges in our culture. The challenges that undermine the traditional or the natural femininity and the new womanhood. And so here is the supreme pursuit for women.

47
00:09:56.574 --> 00:10:09.725
It is equality, career, and independence. That is what the narrative is for women today. Your goal in life: equality, career, and independence. Now, that is a change.

48
00:10:09.725 --> 00:10:16.459
Historically, it has been wife, mother, and complement. Wife, mother, and complement.

49
00:10:16.459 --> 00:10:30.323
So, a huge move away from what we would say the physiology of your body is telling you as a woman that you are all about, and in many ways I would suggest happiness for women.

50
00:10:30.323 --> 00:10:40.068
Steven Clark, the sociologist from Yale University who specializes in the role contributions of men and women, writes this.

51
00:10:40.068 --> 00:10:53.536
He says, "The modern feminist movement, ostensibly a movement for women, normally devalues the thing that women feel the greatest desire to do: to be a wife and a mother.

52
00:10:53.536 --> 00:11:30.694
The effect of the feminist movement has largely made women feel the disadvantage of being female more acutely, and so it puts them under greater pressure to compete with men." In other words, your femininity, your ability to get pregnant, your ability to have kids, this idea that you feel desirous to be in a permanent relationship with a man, that you dream of that kind of romance and intimacy and connectedness and long-term trust, those feelings are your handicap.

53
00:11:30.694 --> 00:11:52.719
And so telling women that what they feel and experience naturally in their biology, in their psychology, and in their spirit puts women in a place where they are encouraged to actually feel bad about who they are unless they can compete and beat out and prove equality with men.

54
00:11:52.719 --> 00:12:08.643
Now, the feminist movement is pretty much in its third wave today. So most people do not feel the feminist movement like what happened in the 1960s. So you kind of say, well, where is this coming from?

55
00:12:08.643 --> 00:12:23.062
Let me just give you some quotes from the first-wave feminist movement so you can get a sense of what happened to form the underpinnings of where your daughters are growing up today.

56
00:12:23.062 --> 00:12:32.490
When it comes to femininity, Betty Friedan's book *The Feminine Mystique* basically broke through and made a statement.

57
00:12:32.490 --> 00:12:53.327
She writes this: once a woman begins to see through the delusions of the feminine mystique, that being feminine is special, she will realize that neither her husband nor her children, nor the things in her home, nor being like any other woman can give her a self.

58
00:12:53.327 --> 00:13:09.806
A self. So the thing she feels and desires and is gifted to do, that is not real. You are not a real person if you do that. You are something less. That makes her a non-person. She calls homemakers parasites.

59
00:13:09.806 --> 00:13:22.086
Homemakers parasites. She calls pregnancy an illness, a disease. Germaine Greer, 1970, in her book *The Female Eunuch*, condemned motherhood as a handicap.

60
00:13:22.086 --> 00:13:31.355
Gloria Steinem later said enlightened women must escape the drudgery and the oppressiveness of the home and husbands.

61
00:13:31.355 --> 00:13:42.605
Simone de Beauvoir said that women should not be allowed to stay home and raise kids because if they are allowed to do so most will choose to.

62
00:13:42.605 --> 00:13:55.043
In other words, the spokesmen for women are saying women should not be allowed to do what they desire to do, what they feel like doing, what they want to do.

63
00:13:55.043 --> 00:14:13.899
And we have raised a whole generation of women being told that really the idea of being married, having a family, raising the next generation, investing in the next generation is somehow beneath you and you will never be happy doing that.

64
00:14:13.899 --> 00:14:25.783
So what does third-wave feminism replace that with? This is very important. You guys get this because this is exactly where your daughters are living.

65
00:14:25.783 --> 00:14:51.373
If my breasts are not to nurse a child, if my uterus produces a monthly swing in my hormones and hygiene issues that I have to take care of, if my vagina is not for me to connect in a permanent relationship with a husband that can produce a child, if that is not what these are for, then what am I supposed to use them for?

66
00:14:51.373 --> 00:15:08.248
You are tuning in, right? What am I supposed to use them for? Okay, so if the greatest pursuit of the new challenge for women is equality, career, and independence, then I am supposed to use my sexuality for what?

67
00:15:08.248 --> 00:15:23.697
To gain equality with men, to gain independence, to develop my career. And so if I have to flirt or sleep my way to the top, I should do that. I need to use this body. I need to flaunt this body.

68
00:15:23.697 --> 00:15:32.174
I can by using my sexuality gain a sense that I have power over people. And we see that in our world today.

69
00:15:32.174 --> 00:15:45.722
And that is why so many women are fighting daily to produce the kind of physical appearance that will somehow earn them status in our culture today. And it is devastating.

70
00:15:45.722 --> 00:15:58.240
Eating disorders, cutting, body hatred among girls. Those things are related to this idea that you are supposed to use your breasts to gain power over people.

71
00:15:58.240 --> 00:16:08.856
And if your body is not shaped right, boy, you are in trouble. You are in trouble. And so that is what is going on in our world today.

72
00:16:08.856 --> 00:16:25.177
Couple books to recommend to you. *The Body Project: An Intimate History of American Girls.* This would be a great one for your wife to read. Be okay for you to read too, but you probably get bored with it.

73
00:16:25.177 --> 00:16:30.326
But a great one for your wife to read, for your daughter to read.

74
00:16:30.326 --> 00:16:47.518
In the 1800s, the majority of the women in America were working on their character by reading the journals and studying what women in their early teens or their late teens and 20s were talking about in their journals.

75
00:16:47.518 --> 00:16:56.866
They were talking about developing their character. But now girls are only talking about how do I make my body better.

76
00:16:56.866 --> 00:17:12.315
And there is a huge financial industry between cosmetics and fashion and hygiene and all of this stuff that money is being made off the pain and suffering of those who do not quite look the part.

77
00:17:12.315 --> 00:17:15.959
And people do not get it. Here is another one.

78
00:17:15.959 --> 00:17:31.646
*A Return to Modesty* by Wendy Shalit, a Jewish girl who writes about how much more fun girls that live in the world of modesty have than girls who flaunt it and have their hearts and worlds broken.

79
00:17:31.646 --> 00:17:46.303
So wild world out there. So what I would add to the new supreme pursuit, equality, career, independence, and now in the third wave, hotness. Being hot is the new pursuit for many women.

80
00:17:46.303 --> 00:17:55.176
So having said that, that is some perspectives. Let me give you a lesson from history there. I put this in here.

81
00:17:55.176 --> 00:18:05.871
We are not going to talk about it but just put this in here so you can see that what is happening in American society is not new to us.

82
00:18:05.871 --> 00:18:22.192
Do not be under the illusion that we have somehow landed at some elite place in the development of humanity. Those who think that just do not read history. You do not read history. You do not know anything.

83
00:18:22.192 --> 00:18:26.787
If you do not think that we have been through this before.

84
00:18:26.787 --> 00:19:14.640
In fact, a classic work by Carl Zimmerman, and no, you cannot borrow my book because it took forever for me to track this down and find it, called *Family and Civilization.* He goes back and studies the family in the rise and fall of various civilizations throughout the history of the world and traces a very similar pattern of how the family is perceived at the beginning of a civilization, what the family is doing during the thriving of a civilization, what happens when the civilization reaches success and the focus of both men and women at that point in time, and then the decline of civilization.

85
00:19:14.640 --> 00:19:25.890
And guess what, folks? We are repeating the exact same pattern of civilizations that fall in the way that we view male roles and female roles.

86
00:19:25.890 --> 00:19:49.658
And so if you read through that section about the Roman family system and its collapse and you substitute America every time you see Rome and you substitute World War II every time you see the Punic Wars in there and read the story, you will be reading a story that you go, that sounds a lot like us.

87
00:19:49.658 --> 00:19:51.717
That sounds a lot like us.

88
00:19:51.717 --> 00:20:04.631
Okay, letter B there. The decline of feminine values training. How does a young girl today grow up with a godly sense of who she is and what is her responsibility?

89
00:20:04.631 --> 00:20:21.268
Where does a girl today grow up being taught what it means to be a woman? Being taught what it means to be feminine. Being taught what it means to have the body that she has and the blessing or benefit of that.

90
00:20:21.268 --> 00:20:38.381
Who is teaching her? Is this something that she is getting from school? Is this something she is getting from college, university? Is this something she is getting from the church? Is she getting this from your wife?

91
00:20:38.381 --> 00:20:43.134
Where is your daughter learning what it means to be a woman?

92
00:20:43.134 --> 00:20:54.542
Let me take you to the New Testament and show you a verse in Titus chapter 2. So Titus is toward the back of the New Testament. Titus chapter 2.

93
00:20:54.542 --> 00:21:01.434
Very interesting passage on where younger women are supposed to get their instructions.

94
00:21:01.434 --> 00:21:26.311
So in Titus chapter 2, starting in verse 3, Titus writes, "Likewise, teach the older women to be reverent in the way they live, not to be slanderers or addicted to much wine, but to teach what is good." If they do that, he says in verse 4, then they can train the younger women to love their husbands and children.

95
00:21:26.311 --> 00:21:41.522
So the younger women here are women who are going to have husbands and children. So we are talking about late adolescence. We are talking about early young adulthood for women, that age group.

96
00:21:41.522 --> 00:21:58.080
The older women are supposed to train them or teach them to love their husbands and their children. Now, some of you would say, "Well, why do you have to teach a woman how to love her husband and her children?

97
00:21:58.080 --> 00:22:15.430
I thought that just came natural. If it is the right mix, if it is a fairy tale marriage, if she finds the right one, will she not just naturally love?" Well, that is predicated on the idea that love is only an emotion.

98
00:22:15.430 --> 00:22:36.267
But if love is greater than an emotion, if it has something to do with self-sacrifice, if it has something to do with understanding what children need, what husbands need, and love is defined as being able to touch people in a way that makes a difference to them.

99
00:22:36.267 --> 00:22:49.577
When you start defining love in the sense of doing good, all of a sudden that requires a bit of information. It requires a bit of training. A bit of help along the way.

100
00:22:49.577 --> 00:23:02.728
Okay, he goes on. He says to be self-controlled and pure, to be busy at home, to be kind, to be subject to their husbands, so that no one will malign the word of God.

101
00:23:02.728 --> 00:23:16.196
In other words, God has a way for both men and women to relate that builds a healthy, God-honoring society and raises up the next generation to be productive God-fearers.

102
00:23:16.196 --> 00:23:20.949
And when we walk away from that design, catastrophe happens.

103
00:23:20.949 --> 00:23:33.863
And the worst thing that happens to a society is when those who call themselves Christians do not follow God's agenda and end up having the same kinds of problems.

104
00:23:33.863 --> 00:23:45.826
The same kinds of divorce, the same kinds of teenage rebellion, the same kinds of addictions to pornography and sex addictions and all of those things.

105
00:23:45.826 --> 00:23:58.740
Same kinds of conflict because we are not just doing what God designed us to do and living that way. And so people go, "Well, what is so unique about Christianity?

106
00:23:58.740 --> 00:24:11.178
It does not seem to help the Christians." He said the word of God would not be maligned. The question is, who is teaching? Who is passing these things along?

107
00:24:11.178 --> 00:24:25.993
Peter Blitchington says this. See, one of the most important characteristics of the mother-daughter relationship is the extent to which it facilitates adequate maternal behavior in girls.

108
00:24:25.993 --> 00:24:41.363
All girls should be taught to understand the critical importance of the maternal role, for one of the more pivotal points upon which a nation rotates is the interaction between mother and child.

109
00:24:41.363 --> 00:24:50.791
We think that the world is going to change based on whether a Democrat or a Republican gets elected to the White House.

110
00:24:50.791 --> 00:25:06.795
But what mothers across this nation are now doing with their five-year-old sons and daughters will actually have a greater impact on this nation than who becomes president. But we do not think that way.

111
00:25:06.795 --> 00:25:15.827
We do not see it that way. And because we do not, that is how a society falls apart. That is why it goes downhill.

112
00:25:15.827 --> 00:25:31.276
He goes on to say, more than training for achievement and competitive skills or social graces, the mother should be concerned with the maternal ability of their girls. So, what is more important?

113
00:25:31.276 --> 00:25:47.676
To teach your girls how to throw a softball or to teach your girls how to love a baby? What is going to make the greatest impact both in the culture and in her personal happiness over the course of her life.

114
00:25:47.676 --> 00:25:54.331
That is kind of strange to even think about because in our culture today, we do not.

115
00:25:54.331 --> 00:26:09.780
We do not think about that in the same way that we do not think about teaching our boys what it means to love a woman, but we do think about what it means to teach them how to kick a soccer ball.

116
00:26:09.780 --> 00:26:18.019
You see, we are missing it a bit. Okay, I am preaching a little bit too much here. I got to keep moving.

117
00:26:18.019 --> 00:26:32.200
So, letter B, the decline of feminine values training. Who is training the women today? Who is training the girls. Third is the rise of the absent mom. The rise of the absent mom.

118
00:26:32.200 --> 00:26:46.698
In 2005, 10 years ago, 59 percent, that is under 60, so 60 percent of children under six were raised with a mom that was working full-time. Now I am not saying that women cannot work.

119
00:26:46.698 --> 00:26:58.899
What I am asking is what happens in the development of children when they miss out on the most important caregiver during their formative years. Well, Dr.

120
00:26:58.899 --> 00:27:15.457
Burton White, the director of the preschool project at Harvard University, you know, a very conservative Christian right-wing institution. Harvard University, right? Here is what he says in regards to daycare.

121
00:27:15.457 --> 00:27:44.375
After more than 30 years of research of how children develop well, "I would not think of putting any infant or toddler of my own into a substitute care program." Now, the reason why you cannot say that out loud, the reason why as a group of men we have to kind of gather clandestinely in these dark corners to have that conversation, is because here is what I hear.

122
00:27:44.375 --> 00:28:00.299
Women say this: I feel like based on our lifestyle and what it takes to get ahead in America, I have got to work full-time. And I do not want you to say that because it makes me feel bad about my kids.

123
00:28:00.299 --> 00:28:17.333
And I do not want to feel that they are not getting the kind of care that they could, because that would say something negative about me. And I do not want to feel that way. So shh, do not say that. Do not say that.

124
00:28:17.333 --> 00:28:34.763
That is why I am telling this to the men, because the men need to listen to this and hear it and think about it because we understand it is not about how you feel. It is actually about what is best for your child, right?

125
00:28:34.763 --> 00:28:50.687
Is that not the goal? Would it not be great if every woman did not have to feel bad because we were not chasing some idealistic American dream. Okay. The rise of the absent mom. Let us keep going here.

126
00:28:50.687 --> 00:28:54.806
Okay. So what do dads contribute to their daughters?

127
00:28:54.806 --> 00:29:08.591
A classic study was done by the Institute for Sexual Research on the role of dads and daughters and what happens if the dad is there and what happens if the dad is not there.

128
00:29:08.591 --> 00:29:24.357
Now you say, let me define there and not there. There means present. There means emotionally there. There means daily interaction. So, dads who are daily present and interacting with their daughters.

129
00:29:24.357 --> 00:29:41.470
Not a part-time dad, not like I am gone Monday through Friday and I show up on the weekends, but dads that are present, regularly there. Here is what they discovered about daughters and women as they were developing.

130
00:29:41.470 --> 00:29:53.116
The first one is this. If he is there, she is very secure being a woman. She is very secure in being a woman. Here is what they came to understand.

131
00:29:53.116 --> 00:30:06.347
That girls gain as much or more understanding about what it means to be feminine by playing off the masculine opposite as they do by relating directly to their mother.

132
00:30:06.347 --> 00:30:23.777
And so when dad is there, girls actually learn, oh that is what masculine is. That is what it feels like. That is what it looks like. I understand masculinity, which makes me more comfortable with my sense of femininity.

133
00:30:23.777 --> 00:30:27.104
They get more comfortable with themselves.

134
00:30:27.104 --> 00:30:43.425
Second, she can easily relate to the opposite sex. She has little problem loving, supporting, and encouraging men. And she functions well in a complementary role because she has actually done that with dad.

135
00:30:43.425 --> 00:30:51.506
She has interacted with him. She has learned how to talk to men. She has learned how to deal with men.

136
00:30:51.506 --> 00:31:01.805
She has learned how to problem-solve with men, which makes her much more capable for the rest of her life in interacting with men.

137
00:31:01.805 --> 00:31:12.263
And that is one of the reasons why God put you in the home, in the family, father, to teach your daughters how to interact with men.

138
00:31:12.263 --> 00:31:18.838
Here is the third one. She will have a highly fulfilling sex life with her husband.

139
00:31:18.838 --> 00:31:35.872
Some of you are saying, "I do not want to write this down because I do not actually want to think about my daughter having sex with anybody." The basis of sexual fulfillment for women starts with the issue of trust.

140
00:31:35.872 --> 00:31:52.906
To give in, which has a lot to do with female satisfaction, with orgasm and things related to sexuality, to be able to surrender to the enjoyment of intercourse with a man. All of that stuff relates to: can I trust?

141
00:31:52.906 --> 00:32:01.145
And an absence of trust because of a lack of a present father creates all kinds of issues for daughters.

142
00:32:01.145 --> 00:32:11.444
And it has a lot to do with how they will experience life, with what they will get out of life, with what they will enjoy in life.

143
00:32:11.444 --> 00:32:28.240
You do not have to go to the Bible to find this out. You can just listen to popular music. John Mayer did a song a few years ago called "Daughters." And in the song, here is what he says. He says, "I know a girl.

144
00:32:28.240 --> 00:32:42.897
She puts the color inside of my world, but she's just like a maze where all of the walls all continually change. And I've done all I can to stand on her steps with my heart in my hands.

145
00:32:42.897 --> 00:32:58.584
Now I'm starting to see maybe it's got nothing to do with me." And then he says this: "Fathers, be good to your daughters. Daughters will love like you do. Girls become lovers who turn into mothers.

146
00:32:58.584 --> 00:33:15.776
So mothers, be good to your daughters too." What is he talking about? He is talking about that well-known phrase that we use all the time called daddy issues. She has got daddy issues. He says, "Oh, you see that skin?

147
00:33:15.776 --> 00:33:30.116
It's the same she's been standing in since the day she saw him walking away. Now she's left cleaning up the mess he made." Daddy issues. That affects a woman's ability to trust men.

148
00:33:30.116 --> 00:33:47.308
In fact, one of the more interesting things about the feminist movement in its original incarnation is if you go back and read the biographies of the early feminists, you will find out that they were not angry at men.

149
00:33:47.308 --> 00:33:59.113
They were angry at a man. Almost every one of the women who were the leaders of the feminist movement had a terrible father. Almost across the board.

150
00:33:59.113 --> 00:34:09.650
Abuse, alcoholism, incest, beating their mother, beating them, and out of that flowed a distrust for all men. A distrust for all men.

151
00:34:09.650 --> 00:34:18.840
Okay. So, if he is not there, here were their general findings. Girls will tend to grow up with one of two extremes.

152
00:34:18.840 --> 00:34:35.477
Either she will be shy, insecure, anxious, and have difficulty bonding with a man in an intimate relationship. So shy, insecure, anxious, difficulty bonding, do not trust men. So I tend to withdraw into myself.

153
00:34:35.477 --> 00:34:45.538
Does not mean she will not marry because she still has the same dreams. But this feeling of isolation, withdrawal, anxiousness.

154
00:34:45.538 --> 00:34:59.719
Or she will tend to be inappropriately self-assertive, sometimes angry, oftentimes promiscuous. Promiscuous, inappropriate, self-assertive, sometimes angry, sometimes promiscuous.

155
00:34:59.719 --> 00:35:16.277
Let me tell you a story really quick. This was one of those eye-opening moments for me. Got a call. A girl in her early 20s wants to come in and see me. So we set the meeting up. She comes in, she is pregnant.

156
00:35:16.277 --> 00:35:28.795
And I said, "Who is the father?" She said, "One-night stand." And I said, "Can I ask you some personal questions?" And she said, "Well, I am here." All right.

157
00:35:28.795 --> 00:35:43.214
And I said, "Okay, well, here goes." So I said, "Why do you do it? Why do you do it? Are you lonely? Do you just like sex? Why do you do one-night stands?" And here is what she said.

158
00:35:43.214 --> 00:35:59.059
She said, "It has nothing to do with liking sex or feeling lonely. It has everything to do with how I see myself." She says, "Sometimes when I am just kind of feeling fat and ugly, I will go to a bar.

159
00:35:59.059 --> 00:36:10.388
I will walk in the bar and I will look around and I will look for who I perceive from my standpoint is one of the best looking guys in the bar.

160
00:36:10.388 --> 00:36:25.995
I will walk up to the guy and I will start flirting with him and before the evening is over, I will proposition him and he will go home with me." She says, "Actually, I have never been turned down.

161
00:36:25.995 --> 00:36:36.770
I have never been turned down." Now, just between us, she is not the most attractive girl I have ever seen, but opportunity to have sex.

162
00:36:36.770 --> 00:36:53.170
She says, "They go home with me, and while they are on top of me, I am thinking to myself, I have got this guy right where I want him. He loves me. He needs me. He is so into me. I am not fat. I am not ugly.

163
00:36:53.170 --> 00:37:06.955
I can have any man I want at any time." And she says, "When it is over, I get up and I say, there is the door. I am done with you." And she said the guys will go like, "What?

164
00:37:06.955 --> 00:37:20.978
That is it?" Because we know, despite the movies, because we did the talk on sex, we know that there is emotional bonding that takes place even for men in a sexual relationship.

165
00:37:20.978 --> 00:37:37.774
And she just runs him out the door and she is laughing the whole way like I can get men to do anything I want them to do. Now the joke is not just on them, it is on her and it is on all people that get into that.

166
00:37:37.774 --> 00:37:52.906
But I thought to myself, how many guys see that girl, that woman in their office who is kind of giving them the wink wink and the nod nod and they are thinking, "Oh, I must be really special.

167
00:37:52.906 --> 00:38:05.740
That woman, she needs somebody like me." Yeah, she might, but it is only for her ego. It is not because of who you are. And guys fall for that stuff all the time.

168
00:38:05.740 --> 00:38:21.031
And all of a sudden in that conversation, it became really real to me that power and anger and promiscuity sometimes are actually weapons that girls who have been broken by men use against men.

169
00:38:21.031 --> 00:38:32.439
They use against men to do some kind of weird thing in their mind and in their heart that is destructive for themselves and for the men as well.

170
00:38:32.439 --> 00:38:48.760
So, what dads can do. Roman numeral number four here. What dads can do. Establish with my wife a firm commitment of what it means to be a real woman. So, what is the definition of what it means to be a man?

171
00:38:48.760 --> 00:38:59.138
We talked about this. Real men reject passivity, accept responsibility, lead courageously, expect the greater reward, God's reward.

172
00:38:59.138 --> 00:39:10.863
And in Rethinking Womanhood, the study that we are doing right now with the women, we unpack a biblical definition for what it means to be feminine.

173
00:39:10.863 --> 00:39:19.419
And in that definition, a real woman is one who, first of all, rejects worldly temptations for significance.

174
00:39:19.419 --> 00:39:39.146
In other words, I am not going to go out and prove to the marketers in the world that I can play for the WNBA or I can close a deal on Wall Street or I can become a PhD just because the world will tell me that I am validated because of those things.

175
00:39:39.146 --> 00:39:52.535
That is not what validates me. I have got gifts and strengths and special abilities. I can do all those things, but I do not have to do them to find my own significance.

176
00:39:52.535 --> 00:40:06.399
Number two, accepts God's design for relationships. Understand that God has designed me to be interdependent with men. Not competing, not against, but interdependent with men.

177
00:40:06.399 --> 00:40:11.231
And that raising the next generation is incredibly important.

178
00:40:11.231 --> 00:40:26.284
For those of you guys who love statistics and love just facts and information, study about the world's population growth in the West and how unsustainable it is for our current civilization.

179
00:40:26.284 --> 00:40:42.842
The reason why that is the case is because we have taught our young women not to have kids. That is what the West is doing. For what stupid reason? Even Darwin knew better than that. Okay guys, think about it.

180
00:40:42.842 --> 00:40:46.486
Think about it. But that is what we have done.

181
00:40:46.486 --> 00:41:02.886
Letter C. Nurtures the next generation. That everything about her tells her that she has got something to contribute and she believes that and leans into that. In 1990, Barbara Bush, the wife of George H. W.

182
00:41:02.886 --> 00:41:18.890
Bush, who was the president of the United States, was invited to speak at Wellesley College commencement. Wellesley College is probably one of the most liberal women's universities in the United States.

183
00:41:18.890 --> 00:41:33.547
And the senior class protested, why would we want to have a wife and a mother come and talk to us? Now today there would be a line of people standing there to not let her on the campus.

184
00:41:33.547 --> 00:41:50.422
The president would lose their job. There would be no free speech available. That is where we have gone since 1990. Great path to travel. But they finally, the college wisely said, no, she is the president's wife.

185
00:41:50.422 --> 00:42:03.177
We are going to have her come speak. And so she came and spoke and had a phenomenal reception when she started talking. But here is what she said in that speech.

186
00:42:03.177 --> 00:42:10.307
She said, the choice, women, that must not be missed is to cherish your human connections.

187
00:42:10.307 --> 00:42:21.795
At the end of your life, you will never regret not having passed one more test, not having won one more verdict, not having closed one more deal.

188
00:42:21.795 --> 00:42:35.501
But you will regret not having spent time with your husband, with your son, and with your daughter. Do not neglect the human connections. So that is what we are encouraging.

189
00:42:35.501 --> 00:42:49.049
Finally, expects God's greater reward. God has rewards in store for those who follow his will. So, first of all, establish with your wife what it means to be a real woman.

190
00:42:49.049 --> 00:42:56.258
So you and your wife will be working with your daughters on the same page. Same definition.

191
00:42:56.258 --> 00:43:12.262
Second, help mom stay home with the children, especially in the critical formative years. In the critical formative years, kids need to get the majority of mommy. They need to get the majority of mommy.

192
00:43:12.262 --> 00:43:17.728
That is not to say a woman cannot earn an income, but think about it.

193
00:43:17.728 --> 00:43:50.290
If you would decide as a man that we are going to bend our economic situation, our spending habits, our lifestyle habits, we are going to bend that around the ability to free up the primary gifted nurturer in our family to give focus and attention particularly in the formative years while the brain is being formed, while the child is learning cognitive ability, things that will last a lifetime in your child.

194
00:43:50.290 --> 00:44:03.045
We are going to prioritize that. We will drive a car that is 10 years old. We will live in a house that does not have a bedroom for every child and every animal.

195
00:44:03.045 --> 00:44:19.128
We will take vacations to Padre or the tent over to Inks Lake. We will just do that because we want to make sure that our kids get the best parenting available. Now, that is so counterintuitive to today.

196
00:44:19.128 --> 00:44:20.712
So counterintuitive.

197
00:44:20.712 --> 00:44:37.429
And so what are we doing? We are raising our girls. We want them all to go to college. We want them all to graduate with $30,000 worth of student loans, of which it is going to take them until age 30 to pay off.

198
00:44:37.429 --> 00:44:41.865
Then they start looking, maybe I need to find a husband.

199
00:44:41.865 --> 00:44:58.106
So by age 33, they found somebody that they are married to, want to wait a couple years before we have kids, and they are 35 and they have their first child and go, wow, we had no idea how awesome this is.

200
00:44:58.106 --> 00:45:12.604
But that is all we can have. Maybe pull one more out because we just put that off because mom and dad told us this is what life ought to look like. This is what it ought to look like.

201
00:45:12.604 --> 00:45:29.162
Mom showed us this is what life ought to look like. This is what we ought to do. So, I am just challenging you guys. Do not just think in terms of what everybody else is believing and doing. Think beyond that.

202
00:45:29.162 --> 00:45:40.729
Letter C. Supports, honors, and cheers for true feminine values in his wife and daughter. You must celebrate those things. Celebrate those things.

203
00:45:40.729 --> 00:45:57.842
It is awesome to be a woman, to be feminine, to be beautiful in who you are, to love children, to love family. It is an awesome thing. You are not just another breadwinner on my way to financial success as a husband.

204
00:45:57.842 --> 00:45:59.981
Family is really important.

205
00:45:59.981 --> 00:46:06.002
Let her date your daughter? Stay involved at a personal level. Talk to them.

206
00:46:06.002 --> 00:46:17.727
You want your daughter's first love to be you, which protects her from falling in love with the first jerk that comes along and shows her attention.

207
00:46:17.727 --> 00:46:38.960
And oftentimes men do not pay attention to their daughter's affection until they are dating somebody or loving somebody and they are thinking to themselves, this is all I get if I want a male's attention, this 16-year-old boy that he loves me, he pays attention to me.

208
00:46:38.960 --> 00:46:50.448
You do not want your daughter's heart to go to him. You want your daughter's heart to be with you. You want your daughter's heart to be with you.

209
00:46:50.448 --> 00:47:07.561
Finally, encourage participation in ceremonies. Now, we are going to take time to walk through all these ceremonies. When we get to next week, we are going to talk about ceremonies for boys and they tend to parallel.

210
00:47:07.561 --> 00:47:23.089
So, I will be talking about this book, *Raising a Modern-Day Knight.* We will be talking about Journey to Manhood. But let me just give you kind of the time frames when good ceremonies take place.

211
00:47:23.089 --> 00:47:39.885
Rites of passage for girls. The first one is around puberty or first period. Most of the time, we are trying to clean up the mess and ignore that that is happening rather than affirming, wow, you are a woman now.

212
00:47:39.885 --> 00:47:56.443
God has given you a gift. It is a beautiful gift. It is the ability to have kids. This is part of who you are becoming. Awesome. Let us celebrate this. Let us celebrate this. You say, "That is weird." Exactly.

213
00:47:56.443 --> 00:48:10.307
Because we have come to think of a woman's body as primarily a sex object. And so the idea that becoming a woman who will be a wife and a mother, that is not the way we think.

214
00:48:10.307 --> 00:48:18.863
And so we do not want to think about a discharge. But this is our daughters, gentlemen. It is our daughters.

215
00:48:18.863 --> 00:48:33.916
Could it be that we have so sexualized women in our thinking that we even kind of project that warped perspective on our little girls? Is that possible? It is a very soul-searching question.

216
00:48:33.916 --> 00:48:50.791
It is time to celebrate that she is becoming a woman. And as a woman, she is not a sex symbol. She is the person that has the ability to bring the next generation to life and continue the beauty of the human race.

217
00:48:50.791 --> 00:48:54.197
Totally different perspective for our kids.

218
00:48:54.197 --> 00:49:11.547
Leaving home. Number two, when it is time for a girl to go out on her own, when she is going off to college or when she is going off to work or when she is going to pursue something outside of home, that is a good time.

219
00:49:11.547 --> 00:49:28.897
The third one, graduation. So, if there is a college, if there is a skill set that she has picked up along the way, taking time along the way to stop and celebrate that. And then the last one is at the time of marriage.

220
00:49:28.897 --> 00:49:38.483
Those are four big pivotal moments in the life of a girl that can be celebrated, can be used to reinforce her femininity.

221
00:49:38.483 --> 00:49:45.138
So, let me leave you with one final quote that I like. I am going to read it to you.

222
00:49:45.138 --> 00:50:01.617
William Maddox writing in the Wall Street Journal on Take Your Daughter to Work Day, he says, I am taking my daughter Allison, 8-year-old, to meet two women who call regularly on members of Congress at lunch.

223
00:50:01.617 --> 00:50:17.938
My daughter is going to talk with a female accountant who also does some public speaking. The afternoon was going to be spent in the company of a woman who once practiced law, now manages a team of writers.

224
00:50:17.938 --> 00:50:25.623
But the best part of Allison's education was going to occur in the car on the way home from work.

225
00:50:25.623 --> 00:50:35.764
Maddox writes, I am sure all of this will be interesting to Allison, but the time I am most looking forward to is the ride home.

226
00:50:35.764 --> 00:50:51.609
For it is then I plan to point out to my daughter that some of the exciting tasks carried out by my female colleagues in the workplace are tasks my wife performed in jobs she held prior to motherhood.

227
00:50:51.609 --> 00:51:04.127
She used to meet regularly with congressmen and senators. She used to do some writing and public speaking. She has a Phi Beta Kappa key from her college days.

228
00:51:04.127 --> 00:51:15.615
After I remind my daughter of these things, I plan to turn to her, look her in the eye, and say, "Allison, you must be a very special young girl.

229
00:51:15.615 --> 00:51:27.420
Your mother could be using her talents and skills in all sorts of jobs in the workplace, but she has chosen instead to use them teaching you at home.

230
00:51:27.420 --> 00:51:45.880
She must love you very, very, very much and think you are very, very important." Somehow I think at that moment my daughter's self-esteem will rise to a level heretofore unimagined by the organizers of Take Your Daughter to Work Day.

231
00:51:45.880 --> 00:51:57.130
And for that I owe a debt of gratitude to my wife whose esteem-building job as a mother at home rarely receives the public esteem it deserves.

232
00:51:57.130 --> 00:52:13.000
Gentlemen, if we could get back to those days, we have a chance to turn our nation around and bring happiness to the females in our world again. Okay, I think we are going to have our discussion now.
